WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.140
Bismillah wa alhamdulillah wa sallallahu alaihi
wa sallam wa ala rasulullah. Hello

00:00:02.990 --> 00:00:06.060
calculus students, today we're going to be
taking derivatives using implicit

00:00:05.910 --> 00:00:11.030
differentiation. Let's get into it. On to our first
example here, we have x cubed plus y

00:00:10.880 --> 00:00:15.490
cubed equals 9, and we have to find dy
over dx. So when we're implicit

00:00:15.340 --> 00:00:20.590
differentiating, we have to use our
Leibniz notation. For our

00:00:20.440 --> 00:00:25.750
equation here, we will have d of x cubed

00:00:25.600 --> 00:00:30.450
over dx plus d of y cubed over

00:00:30.300 --> 00:00:34.490
dx equals d of 9 over dx.

00:00:35.900 --> 00:00:39.690
For our first term, this is just the exact
same as if we applied the power rule

00:00:39.540 --> 00:00:44.350
because we're deriving x cubed with respect to
the same variable with respect to x.

00:00:44.320 --> 00:00:48.930
So this just becomes 3x squared. And then let's
leave this guy for one second. Let's

00:00:48.780 --> 00:00:53.310
go to our third term. We're deriving a constant
with respect to x. If we derive the

00:00:53.160 --> 00:00:58.460
constant with respect to any variable, it's
always going to be 0. And then for our

00:00:58.310 --> 00:01:03.840
middle term, because we're not deriving y with
y, we're deriving y with a different

00:01:03.690 --> 00:01:09.140
variable, we have to first do d of y
cubed over dy times

00:01:08.990 --> 00:01:14.640
dy over dx. Using our chain rule,
this will then become 3x

00:01:14.490 --> 00:01:19.800
squared [plus] 3y squared dy
over dx equals 0.

00:01:19.930 --> 00:01:25.260
We bring this y over the 0 and multiply it by
negative 1. It becomes 3x squared,

00:01:25.110 --> 00:01:29.920
minus... equals negative [3]y squared dy over

00:01:29.770 --> 00:01:34.620
dx. Divide [by] negative

00:01:34.470 --> 00:01:39.780
3y squared on both sides, we will get
negative 3x squared over

00:01:40.370 --> 00:01:45.530
3y squared equals dy

00:01:45.380 --> 00:01:50.790
over dx. Then we have dy over dx equals

00:01:50.640 --> 00:01:55.880
negative x squared over y squared.

00:01:56.290 --> 00:02:01.140
Now on to our next example. We have 3 square
root of x plus 2 over y equals 4. And

00:02:00.990 --> 00:02:04.960
we have to find the tangent at 1, 2. To find the
tangent, we have to first find the

00:02:04.810 --> 00:02:09.120
slope. And to find the slope, we have to find dy
over dx. So once again, we're going

00:02:08.970 --> 00:02:13.740
to solve this using implicit
differentiation, using our Leibniz notation.

00:02:14.350 --> 00:02:19.950
We can apply the d over dx to

00:02:19.800 --> 00:02:20.810
each of these terms.

00:02:21.560 --> 00:02:25.430
For our first term, we can take the 3 out and
then change that square root to a

00:02:25.280 --> 00:02:30.390
power of half. So we're going to have
d of x to the half over dx,

00:02:30.580 --> 00:02:36.210
plus take that 2 out as well. And then we're
going to have d of y to the negative

00:02:36.060 --> 00:02:41.650
1 over dy multiplied by dy over dx. And

00:02:41.500 --> 00:02:46.270
then for our last term, we're going
to have d of 4 over dx.

00:02:47.190 --> 00:02:52.800
This is just our power rule. We're
going to get 3 times 1 over 2x

00:02:52.650 --> 00:02:58.180
to the negative 1 over 2 plus 2. Power,
again, applying to that y

00:02:58.030 --> 00:03:03.260
to the negative 1 is going to give us
negative y to the negative 2 dy

00:03:03.110 --> 00:03:04.340
over dx.

00:03:05.470 --> 00:03:10.780
And then applying the derivative to 4, we'll get
a 0 because 4 is a constant. This

00:03:10.630 --> 00:03:16.280
will give us 3 over 2x to the
negative 1 over 2. And then

00:03:16.130 --> 00:03:19.000
we're going to bring this to the other side.
So that negative will become a

00:03:18.850 --> 00:03:24.020
positive. So this will become equals 2y
to the negative 2 dy over dx.

00:03:25.970 --> 00:03:31.450
Divide this by 2y [to the negative 2] on both
sides. We'll get 3

00:03:31.300 --> 00:03:33.650
over 4x

00:03:35.030 --> 00:03:40.400
to the negative 1 over 2y to the
negative 2 equals dy over dx.

00:03:41.050 --> 00:03:44.760
Because these are both negative, we can just
switch their spots. So that will be

00:03:44.610 --> 00:03:48.680
equal to, so dy over dx will equal

00:03:48.530 --> 00:03:54.120
3y squared over 4 root x because
this half will turn

00:03:53.970 --> 00:03:54.680
into a root.

00:03:55.350 --> 00:04:00.440
Now that we have dy over dx, we can
plug in our point 1, 2.

00:04:00.290 --> 00:04:05.620
Plugging in our point 1, 2 will
give us dy over dx

00:04:05.470 --> 00:04:10.090
is equal to 3 times

00:04:09.940 --> 00:04:11.330
2

00:04:11.980 --> 00:04:17.550
squared over 4 times root of 1, which
is just 1. That equals

00:04:17.400 --> 00:04:20.440
12 over 4, which equals 3.

00:04:21.530 --> 00:04:26.900
Now we have our m and we have two
points. We can plug them in to

00:04:26.750 --> 00:04:31.940
our m equals y2 minus y1 over x2 minus

00:04:31.790 --> 00:04:36.160
x1, which is 3 equals y minus

00:04:38.060 --> 00:04:43.470
2 over x minus 1. That gives us 3x

00:04:43.320 --> 00:04:48.750
minus 3 equals y minus 2. So we have 3x

00:04:48.600 --> 00:04:49.630
minus y

00:04:50.760 --> 00:04:56.290
minus 1 equals 0 as the equation
of our tangent at

00:04:56.140 --> 00:05:01.460
point (1, 2). On to our last example, we
have x squared times y

00:05:01.310 --> 00:05:06.340
plus x times y squared equals 5. And once
again, we have to find dy over dx.

00:05:06.810 --> 00:05:12.460
Here, we'll just start by applying our
derivative. So we'll have d of x

00:05:12.540 --> 00:05:18.030
squared y over dx plus d of xy squared

00:05:17.880 --> 00:05:23.350
over dx equals d of 5 over

00:05:23.200 --> 00:05:27.670
dx. Here, though, it's going to be a little
bit different because since both of

00:05:27.520 --> 00:05:32.250
these variables are eventually going to be in
terms of dx, because here we send y to

00:05:32.100 --> 00:05:36.150
dx when we multiply it by dy over dx, or in this
example, we have the same thing by

00:05:36.000 --> 00:05:41.630
sending dy over dx. So y is going
to be in a product

00:05:41.480 --> 00:05:46.930
rule with x squared. So this is going to be
the same as doing d of x squared

00:05:46.780 --> 00:05:52.050
over dx times y plus x squared times

00:05:51.900 --> 00:05:57.550
dy over dx. And then that's going to be

00:05:57.400 --> 00:06:01.570
our first bracket. And we're going to have the
second bracket is going to be plus

00:06:01.870 --> 00:06:06.670
dx over dx

00:06:07.380 --> 00:06:12.330
times y squared plus x

00:06:12.180 --> 00:06:17.750
times d of y squared over dx. And this is
all equal to 0 once we

00:06:17.600 --> 00:06:18.830
apply the derivative to 5.

00:06:19.570 --> 00:06:24.840
Doing the power rule to our first one, we
will get 2x times y, so 2xy,

00:06:24.690 --> 00:06:29.840
and then plus x squared. And then
because we have here dy over dx,

00:06:29.970 --> 00:06:35.460
we're going to do dy over dy times dy
over dx, which is just dy

00:06:35.310 --> 00:06:37.700
over dx. So we're going to just
kind of do the same.

00:06:38.580 --> 00:06:44.110
And then for our next two, we're going to
have dx over dx, which is 1, times

00:06:43.960 --> 00:06:49.530
y squared. So it's going to be plus y
squared, plus x times d of y squared

00:06:49.380 --> 00:06:54.590
over dx. That's going to be d of y squared over
dy times dy over dx, which is

00:06:54.570 --> 00:06:58.960
x times 2y dy over dx.

00:06:59.860 --> 00:07:04.480
Here we have 2xy plus y squared.

00:07:05.300 --> 00:07:09.470
We can put it on one side because they have no
dy's over dx's. Then on the other

00:07:09.320 --> 00:07:10.850
side, we can have plus

00:07:12.200 --> 00:07:17.850
2xy plus x squared, and we can
factor out the dy over

00:07:17.700 --> 00:07:19.610
dx, and this all equals 0.

00:07:22.180 --> 00:07:27.090
Lastly, we move that to the other side. We're
going to get 2xy plus y squared

00:07:27.100 --> 00:07:32.530
equals negative 2xy plus

00:07:32.580 --> 00:07:37.670
x or minus x squared all dy over dx.

00:07:37.780 --> 00:07:42.350
Bring that under, we get 2xy
plus y squared

00:07:42.770 --> 00:07:47.940
over negative 2xy minus x

00:07:47.790 --> 00:07:52.260
squared equals dy over dx.

00:07:53.710 --> 00:07:57.000
So as you can see, it's pretty easy. It's just
like a very small pattern that we

00:07:56.850 --> 00:08:01.400
have to do whenever we interact with a y term
because we're not deriving with

00:08:01.250 --> 00:08:06.500
respect to y. We're deriving with respect to x.
If instead we were deriving with

00:08:06.350 --> 00:08:10.320
respect to y, the process that we're taking
would be the same. We're just doing it

00:08:10.170 --> 00:08:15.260
to x instead. It's pretty easy, but we just have
to understand this quickly before

00:08:15.110 --> 00:08:20.660
we go to our next topic in the unit, which
is related rates. I will see you

00:08:20.510 --> 00:08:21.480
guys in the next one.
